<title>JAPAN: JAL slips on glum earnings forecast.</title>
<headline>JAL slips on glum earnings forecast.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Japan Airlines Co Ltd slipped to a fresh low for the year in Monday morning trade, after the firm announced a glum earnings forecast late last week, brokers said.</p>
<p>By 0047 GMT, the shares had fallen six yen to 480 yen, one yen under the previous low set on January 28.  </p>
<p>On Friday, JAL said it had revised its parent current forecast for 1996/97 to a loss of 20.00 billion yen, down from a previous forecast of neither a profit nor a loss.</p>
